  "text": "Q: My co-founder just told an investor that our burn rate is aggressive but spiritual. Should I be worried? Hmm. I'd be a little concerned, and I'd use it as a cue to steer the message back to facts. Spiritual sounds flippant, and investors want clear signals. So just reset the frame. Try, \"We're investing ahead of revenue, but we have a handle on it.\" Haha. Okay, okay. So how do I explain burn properly next time? Start with a number, monthly burn and runway. Then explain why it's at that level, hiring, growth bets, whatever's driving it. Close with what you're doing to manage it, specific milestones, and what you'd trim if you had to. It shows control and discipline without killing the story.",
